Nivel de vechime: Începător
Tip de angajare: Full-time
Sectoare de activitate: Dezvoltare de software
About us 
 Integrisoft is a software company established in 1999, focused on product development, custom software, and solutions for public administration. We are the leading provider of local tax software solutions in Romania.
 Our team is growing, and we’re looking for a .NET Developer with 2-4 years of experience to join the team responsible for maintaining and continuously improving one of our established software products.
 This is a great opportunity for a developer who wants to take real ownership of an enterprise application used in real-world business processes, work alongside an experienced team, and have a direct impact on the product’s quality and evolution.
 Who you are 
2-4 years of professional experience in software development using C# and .NET;
Graduate of a degree in Computer Science, Informatics, Cybernetics, Automation, or other related field (or equivalent practical experience);
Solid understanding of Object-Oriented Programming, design principles, and good coding practices;
Comfortable working with large existing codebases and quickly understanding business logic;
Able to investigate complex issues independently and identify root causes;
Structured and analytical approach to problem solving;
Attention to detail and a quality-oriented mindset;
Good communication and teamwork skills, with the ability to explain technical topics clearly;
Responsible, organized, and proactive.
 What you'll do 
 As a .NET Developer, you will play an active role in the maintenance and continuous improvement of an established enterprise software application, working independently on tasks of medium to high complexity.
 Your responsibilities will include:
Analyzing reported issues, identifying root causes, and implementing reliable fixes;
Designing and implementing new features and enhancements;
Developing, maintaining, and refactoring application modules;
Working with C#, ASP.NET, and WebForms;
Writing and optimizing SQL queries, stored procedures, and database structures in Microsoft SQL Server;
Developing and maintaining reports in SQL Server Reporting Services (SSRS);
Working with web technologies such as JavaScript, jQuery, and AJAX;
Integrating with internal and external systems through Web Services / APIs;
Testing and debugging your changes and ensuring code quality;
Participating in code reviews and contributing to technical decisions;
Taking part in the entire process, from requirements analysis and estimation to development, testing, and deployment;
Writing and maintaining technical documentation;
Supporting and guiding junior colleagues when needed;
Collaborating closely with other developers, testers, and team members.
 Requirements 
2-4 years of hands-on experience with C# and .NET;
Practical experience with ASP.NET (WebForms experience is a strong plus);
Good knowledge of SQL and Microsoft SQL Server (queries, joins, stored procedures, basic performance optimization);
Good knowledge of HTML, CSS, and JavaScript;
Experience with jQuery and AJAX;
Experience working with Web Services / APIs (SOAP and/or REST);
Experience with version control systems (Git and/or TFVC);
Experience maintaining or extending an existing application;
Strong analytical thinking and problem-solving skills.
 Nice to have 
Experience with SQL Server Reporting Services (SSRS);
Familiarity with Azure DevOps Server (work items, pipelines, repositories);
Experience with Agile methodologies (Scrum / Kanban);
Experience with performance tuning of SQL queries or web applications;
Knowledge of .NET Core / modern .NET;
Experience with applications for public administration or similar business domains;
Experience mentoring or onboarding junior developers.
 Tech stack 
 Backend: C#, ASP.NET, WebForms, Web Services / APIs 
Frontend: JavaScript, jQuery, AJAX, HTML, CSS
Database: Microsoft SQL Server
Reporting: SQL Server Reporting Services (SSRS)
Version control: Git and TFVC
DevOps: Azure DevOps Server (on-premises)
Development: Visual Studio
 What we offer 
Real ownership over modules and features of an established enterprise product;
Opportunities for professional growth and increasing technical responsibility;
An experienced team and a culture of knowledge sharing;
Exposure to the complete software development lifecycle;
Friendly and collaborative working environment;
Team-building activities;
Private healthcare through MedLife;
Tea and coffee;
Fruit Days 🍎;
Short Friday.
 Work mode 
 Full-time 
Hybrid
Office located near Obor Square, Bucharest – 5-minute walk from Obor metro station 
 If you’re an experienced .NET developer looking for a stable environment where your work has real impact on software used in real-world business processes, we’d love to meet you. 
 Come and join Integrisoft!
